/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  Temperature BC of the opaque front and back faces of the porous zone
  (front x = 75 mm, back x = 125 mm). Included on BOTH sides of BOTH faces:
     0/inletRegion/T   inletRegion_to_porousRegion
     0/porousRegion/T  porousRegion_to_inletRegion, porousRegion_to_exitRegion
     0/exitRegion/T    exitRegion_to_porousRegion
  The ray BC on all four patches must be greyDiffusiveRadiation (only that BC books qin/qr:
  greyDiffusiveRadiationMixedFvPatchScalarField.C:181, 336-362).

  Face balance (paper 2, Eq. bc_interface; T continuous; net radiation absorbed on both sides):
     k1 (Tc1 - Tf) + k2 (Tc2 - Tf) + Qabs - E Tf^4 = 0
     k      = kappa*deltaCoeffs of each side (kappa_f or kappa_con, from that region's thermo)
     Qabs   = (1 - c1(1-eps1)) qin1 + (1 - c2(1-eps2)) qin2     (qin: fvDOM incident flux, beam incl.)
     E      = (c1 eps1 + c2 eps2) sigma
     c      = sum over the rays LEAVING the face on that side of (-n.dAve)/pi, computed from that
              region's own fvDOM rays and its own patch normals (same test and weight as
              greyDiffusive, lines 212 and 336-351); 0.99145 (cos 7.5 deg) on these faces for 6 x 11
     eps    = emissivity of that side from constant/<region>/boundaryRadiationProperties, i.e.
              exactly the value the greyDiffusive rays use (line 186-191)
  With c and eps taken from the radiation model itself, Qabs - E Tf^4 equals fvDOM's
  qr(side 1) + qr(side 2) at convergence: the face creates and destroys no energy.

  Only qin is explicit (frozen between ray solves). Emission is implicit: Newton on
  f(T) = C - K T - E T^4 (decreasing, concave) from the upper bound min(C/K, (C/E)^1/4) converges
  monotonically; the mixed coefficients are the tangent at T* with this side's cell implicit:
     a = k2 + 4 E T*^3,  b = k2 Tc2 + Qabs + 3 E T*^4
     refValue = b/a,  valueFraction = a/(a + k1),  refGradient = 0   =>  Tf = (k1 Tc1 + b)/(k1 + a)
  Both sides solve the same balance, so they hold the same Tf at convergence.
  h follows through mixedEnergy (mixedEnergyFvPatchScalarField.C:103-128).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

type            codedMixed;
name            radiativeInterfaceT;

refValue        uniform 300;
refGradient     uniform 0;
valueFraction   uniform 1;
value           uniform 300;

